course: dictionary
lesson: 2856
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Near the equator lies a zone of weak, changing winds called the doldrums, where sailing ships could be stuck for days.» The clues are winds, sailing ships and stuck for days, so the doldrums here is a place at sea.
explain: Doldrums is a noun, and it is often used with «the». In everyday talk, «in the doldrums» means feeling fed up, bored or stuck, with no energy. «The economy is in the doldrums» means something is not doing well and is not growing.
explain: To choose the right meaning, try each one in the sentence and see which makes sense. Ask yourself: is this about a place, a feeling, or a time when nothing is happening? The check works for every word with more than one meaning.
fact: Doldrums has three meanings: a feeling of being sad, bored or stuck; a time when nothing is happening or growing; and an area of sea near the equator with very little wind.
fact: «In the doldrums» means feeling fed up or stuck, with no energy.
fact: «The economy is in the doldrums» means it is not doing well and is not growing.
fact: In geography, the doldrums are an area of sea near the equator where there is often very little wind, so sailing ships could be stuck for days.
fact: In «The Phantom Tollbooth» the hero gets stuck in the Doldrums, a place where thinking is not allowed.
exercise: «Near the equator lies a zone of weak, changing winds called the doldrums, where sailing ships could be stuck for days.» What are the doldrums in this sentence? | A strong wind near the poles | *A part of the sea near the equator with little wind | A type of sailing ship | A feeling of being fed up
exercise: Mia says, «I'm in the doldrums since the rain started.» What does she mean? | She is sailing a ship through a storm | She is very excited about the rain | She is standing on the equator | *She is feeling fed up and stuck
exercise: «The economy is in the doldrums.» Which meaning fits best? | A calm sea near the equator | Prices are very high | Everyone is very excited | *A time when nothing is growing or doing well
test: «The sailing ship drifted for days in the doldrums.» Which meaning fits? | A very fast wind | A kind of food | *A calm area of sea with very little wind | A sad feeling
test: «Dan has been in the doldrums all week since his best friend moved away.» Which meaning fits? | A type of ship | *A feeling of being sad and stuck | A time when nothing is growing | A place at sea near the equator
exam: Which sentence uses doldrums to mean a feeling of being fed up? | The ship was stuck in the doldrums for three days | *Ella has been in the doldrums since her friend moved away | The doldrums lie near the equator, where the winds are weak | The winds were weak and changing
